      \item PDE: wavelength-dependent (AFBR-S4N66P024M curve)
      \item Mean PDE over detected photons: 0.607 (selection-biased)
    \end{itemize}

    \column{0.41\linewidth}
    \textbf{A2 — R=0.95 vs R=0.98}\\[4pt]
    Code value (Materials.cc): $R = 0.95$\\
    Manufacturer Vikuiti ESR spec: $R \approx 0.98$\\[4pt]
    The code comment says ``R=0.98 Vikuiti ESR'' but the actual constant set is 0.95.
    All simulation results in this analysis use \alert{$R=0.95$}.\\[6pt]
    \textbf{Napkin uses $R=0.98$} for reflector attenuation estimates.
    The $\Lambda_\text{refl}$ values assume R=0.98.
    With R=0.95: $\Lambda_\text{refl}^H = 240\mm$ (shorter — more loss).\\[4pt]
    This discrepancy should be corrected in a future simulation campaign.
  \end{columns}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{A3 — Air-Gap Geometry Details}
  \begin{columns}[T]
    \column{0.52\linewidth}
    \textbf{GEN-3 volume hierarchy:}
    \begin{itemize}\setlength\itemsep{2pt}
      \item \texttt{WorldLV} $\supset$ \texttt{BarLV} (EJ-230)
      \item \texttt{BarLV} surrounded by \texttt{AirGapLV} (0.10 mm each side)
      \item \texttt{AirGapLV} surrounded by \texttt{MylarLV} (0.05 mm)
